    "title": "Wiz Player",
    "description": "Wiz Player | Video Player, a lifestyle app crafted by Sneig, offers a diverse content experience, embracing live-streamed events and providing access to movies and music. This IPTV player supports streaming through Xtream, M3U, and FG codes, boasting an intuitive interface for seamless content consumption. Noteworthy features include background playback, the ability to save favorite channels, and simultaneous channel playback. Enhancing social interaction, the app facilitates chat with friends and family, supports content sharing, and allows casting to TVs via Web Video Caster and Miracast. Choose from SD, HD, FHD, and 4k video qualities, and relish uninterrupted streaming with exceptional quality, making it an ideal choice for hassle-free content enjoyment across a global spectrum.\r\nDelving deeper into Wiz Player | Video Player, the app's versatility shines through its grid or list view organization of channels, adapting to user preferences seamlessly. The user-friendly interface ensures effortless navigation to find desired shows, movies, and channels. As you indulge in content, the background playback feature enables multitasking, letting you explore other apps without interrupting your viewing experience.\r\n\r\nA standout attribute lies in the app's capability to support FG code, Xtream, and M3U URLs, providing access to a vast array of global content. Whether you opt for the smooth playback of SD, the clarity of HD, the sharpness of FHD, or the immersive experience of 4k quality, Wiz Player ensures a tailored viewing experience.\r\n\r\nWith its commitment to uninterrupted streaming, this IPTV player stands out for its reliability, making it a go-to choice for those who prioritize seamless content consumption. Wiz Player | Video Player redefines the boundaries of mobile entertainment by seamlessly integrating social interactions, content sharing, and high-quality streaming, establishing itself as a comprehensive and user-centric lifestyle application.\r\nAs far as we know a link reader does not directly infringe copyright because no copying is made on the app's servers, so this is not a valid reason to send a DMCA notice. To remove this content from the web, the content owner must contact the host who actually hosts the content (not the people responsible for this application).\r\nAt Drama Live, we are prepared to ban any server address if we receive a complaint that it is serving illegal content to wizgan2013@gmail.com",
